  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Grandhi Veerabhadra Rao, vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh,",
    "facts": "It is contended that the jiggery is treated as agricultural produce, the petitioner has valid registration from the GST and Food Safety Authorities in India. However officials of the respondent have seized 17,919 KGs. of jaggery from the petitioner in connection with Cr. No.98 of 2025 dated 21.04.2025 for offences under 7-B r/w 8-A & B of A.P. Prohibition Act, 1995 (Amended 2020).",
    "arguments": "It is further contended that the possession and sale of jaggery cannot be viewed as an offence under the provisions of AP Excise Act. It is further argued that the stock has been lying with the respondents since 21.04.2025, which is perishable item, prays for release of the same. The learned counsel relies on the Division Bench decision of this Court in W.P. No.12429 of 2022.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is further contended that the possession and sale of jaggery cannot be viewed as an offence under the provisions of AP Excise Act. It is further argued that the stock has been lying with the respondents since 21.04.2025, which is perishable item, prays for release of the same. The learned counsel relies on the Division Bench decision of this Court in W.P. No.12429 of 2022.",
